    <title>Scaling Test-Time Compute with
      Process Reward Models for Mathematical Reasoning</title>
    <summary>  Large language models struggle with multi-step problems. We propose a process reward model that
      scores each reasoning step and allocates test-time compute adaptively. Our method improves accuracy on
      GSM8K and MATH500 by 6.1 points over self-consistency while using 40% fewer samples.
    </summary>
    <author><name>Ada Lovelace</name></author>
    <author><name>Alan Turing</name></author>
